  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    ACTS Common Course - MATH 2203.\n\nPrerequisite: A math ACT score of 22 or above or a C or above MATH 1113. \n\nAn introduction to the concepts of differentiation and integration. Emphasis will be placed on applications of calculus in business, economics, accounting, social sciences, and life sciences. \n\nNote: A grade of C of better must be earned in this course if being used to satisfy the general education mathematics requirement. May not be taken for credit after completion of MATH 2914 or equivalent.\n    \n</section>",
